  <!-- EDUCATIONAL SEO ARTICLE SLOT (Styled matching age.astro) -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="gpa-content">
      <h2>GPA Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>GPA Calculator</strong> is a versatile academic tool built for college and high school students to compute their Grade Point Average, evaluate cumulative GPA across semesters, compare weighted vs unweighted scores, plan target semester goals, and convert percentage marks to standard GPA scales.
      </p>

      <h2>What Is a GPA Calculator?</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>Grade Point Average (GPA)</strong> is a standardized numeric metric used by schools, universities, scholarship committees, and graduate admissions to summarize a student's academic performance across all completed courses.
      </p>

      <h2>How Does a College GPA Calculator Work?</h2>
      <p>
        In collegiate semester systems, GPA is calculated using <strong>Quality Points</strong>:
      </p>
      <div class="my-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100/80 p-4 font-mono text-sm dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
        <div>1. Quality Points for a Course = Credit Hours × Grade Points</div>
        <div class="mt-1 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">2. Semester GPA = Total Quality Points ÷ Total Credit Hours</div>
      </div>
      <p>
        <strong>Worked Example:</strong> If you take <em>Math (4 credits, grade A = 4.0)</em> and <em>Physics (3 credits, grade B+ = 3.3)</em>:
        <br />
        <code>Quality Points = (4 × 4.0) + (3 × 3.3) = 16.0 + 9.9 = 25.9 points</code>.
        <br />
        <code>Total Credits = 4 + 3 = 7 credits</code>.
        <br />
        <code>College GPA = 25.9 ÷ 7 = 3.70</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>College GPA Calculator vs High School GPA Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        While both metrics measure student success, high schools and colleges differ in course weights and credit units:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>College GPA:</strong> Courses carry variable credit weights (typically 1 to 5 credit hours), and difficulty weighting is rarely applied to the base GPA.</li>
        <li><strong>High School GPA:</strong> Courses generally carry equal credit weight (1.0 per year), but course rigor levels (Honors, Advanced Placement, IB) earn weighted bonus points.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Weighted GPA vs Unweighted GPA</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Unweighted GPA:</strong> Measured on a strict <code>4.0 scale</code> regardless of course difficulty (an A in standard art equals an A in AP Physics).
        <br />
        <strong>Weighted GPA:</strong> Gives additional grade points for advanced courses:
        <br />
        <code>Honors Classes: +0.5 Bonus (A = 4.5)</code>
        <br />
        <code>AP / Advanced Classes: +1.0 Bonus (A = 5.0)</code>
      </p>

      <h2>How to Calculate Cumulative GPA</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>cumulative GPA calculator</strong> combines previous credit history with a newly completed semester:
      </p>
      <div class="my-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100/80 p-4 font-mono text-sm dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
        <div>Cumulative GPA = [(Current GPA × Prior Credits) + (New GPA × New Credits)] ÷ (Prior Credits + New Credits)</div>
      </div>

      <h2>Percentage to GPA Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        International universities and Indian academic boards frequently report marks as percentages or 10-point CGPA. Our <strong>percentage to GPA calculator</strong> provides both simple linear proportional scaling and collegiate bracket mapping.
      </p>

      <h2>VIT GPA Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Students frequently search for a <em>vit gpa calculator</em> to estimate semester GPA and CGPA using credit weights and 10-point grading scales (S, A, B, C, D, E, F).
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 italic">
        * Notice: This is an independent calculator tool. Academic regulations, grade-point allocations, and credit rules vary by program, batch, and institution. This tool is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Vellore Institute of Technology (VIT).
      </p>

      <h2>MIT GPA Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Students searching for an <em>mit gpa calculator</em> often look for 5.0 scale conversion matrices (A = 5, B = 4, C = 3).
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 italic">
        * Notice: This calculator is an independent educational tool and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT).
      </p>

      <h2>Standard 4.0 GPA Scale Reference Table</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-900 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-bold">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-2.5">Letter Grade</th>
              <th class="p-2.5">Standard 4.0 Points</th>
              <th class="p-2.5">Weighted Honors (4.5)</th>
              <th class="p-2.5">Weighted AP (5.0)</th>
              <th class="p-2.5">Example Percentage</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-mono">
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">A+</td><td class="p-2">4.0</td><td class="p-2">4.5</td><td class="p-2">5.0</td><td class="p-2">97–100%</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">A</td><td class="p-2">4.0</td><td class="p-2">4.5</td><td class="p-2">5.0</td><td class="p-2">93–96%</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">A-</td><td class="p-2">3.7</td><td class="p-2">4.2</td><td class="p-2">4.7</td><td class="p-2">90–92%</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">B+</td><td class="p-2">3.3</td><td class="p-2">3.8</td><td class="p-2">4.3</td><td class="p-2">87–89%</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">B</td><td class="p-2">3.0</td><td class="p-2">3.5</td><td class="p-2">4.0</td><td class="p-2">83–86%</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">B-</td><td class="p-2">2.7</td><td class="p-2">3.2</td><td class="p-2">3.7</td><td class="p-2">80–82%</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">C+</td><td class="p-2">2.3</td><td class="p-2">2.8</td><td class="p-2">3.3</td><td class="p-2">77–79%</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">C</td><td class="p-2">2.0</td><td class="p-2">2.5</td><td class="p-2">3.0</td><td class="p-2">73–76%</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">D</td><td class="p-2">1.0</td><td class="p-2">1.5</td><td class="p-2">2.0</td><td class="p-2">60–69%</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-2 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">F</td><td class="p-2">0.0</td><td class="p-2">0.0</td><td class="p-2">0.0</td><td class="p-2">Below 60%</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
  </Fragment>

  <!-- FAQ SECTION SLOT (EXACTLY 7 FAQs AS REQUIRED) -->
  <Fragment slot="faq">
    <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
      
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800" open>
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            1. How do I calculate my GPA?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Multiply each course's credit hours by its earned grade points to get quality points. Add up all quality points and divide by your total credit hours: <code>GPA = Total Quality Points ÷ Total Credits</code>.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            2. How does a college GPA calculator work?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          A college GPA calculator factors in variable credit weights per class (e.g. 3 or 4 credit courses) and maps letter grades on a standard 4.0 scale to determine semester standing.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            3. What is the difference between weighted and unweighted GPA?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Unweighted GPA evaluates all classes on a 4.0 scale regardless of difficulty. Weighted GPA awards extra points (+0.5 for Honors, +1.0 for AP/IB) resulting in scales up to 5.0.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            4. How do I calculate my cumulative GPA?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Multiply previous cumulative GPA by completed credits, add new semester quality points, and divide by the total combined credit hours.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            5. Can I convert percentage to GPA?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Yes. Use our "Percentage to GPA" tab to convert marks to a 4.0, 5.0, or 10.0 scale using simple linear or bracket grade mapping.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            6. Is the GPA scale the same for every college and high school?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          No. While the 4.0 scale is widespread in North America, many universities and high schools customize plus/minus values, honors bonuses, or 5.0 / 10.0 scale mappings.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            7. Can I use this calculator for VIT, MIT, or another university?
